            <ArticleTitle>Case of the Massachusetts General Hospital: Case 35-2013: a 77-year-old man with confusion and malaise.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1946-57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1056/NEJMcpc1209274</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 77-year-old man was admitted to this hospital because of confusion and malaise after resection of a papillary urothelial cancer. He reported abdominal pain, facial and jaw pain, anorexia, lethargy, weakness, and night sweats; imaging revealed generalized lymphadenopathy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
